(3203371, 448663, 71770, '<td valign="top">i love black cats!</td>', 'i love black cats!', '2007-01-10 01:12:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3203374, 450805, 19982, '<td valign="top">She''s pretty and all, but...  see how the light on her sleeve is brighter than the light on her face?  It draws the attention away from her face.  Also, her sleeve appears as if it could be in sharper focus than her eyes.  The eyes are critical for getting the portrait right.  If this was made with available light, I''d probably darken the sleeve in post processing, and lighten the face, especially the eyes and teeth.  If you had supplemental lighting available, it would have been better to get the exposure closer in camera.</td>', 'She''s pretty and all, but...  see how the light on her sleeve is brighter than the light on her face?  It draws the attention away from her face.  Also, her sleeve appears as if it could be in sharper focus than her eyes.  The eyes are critical for getting the portrait right.  If this was made with available light, I''d probably darken the sleeve in post processing, and lighten the face, especially the eyes and teeth.  If you had supplemental lighting available, it would have been better to get the exposure closer in camera.', '2007-01-10 01:12:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(3203375, 447207, 69121, '<td valign="top">Either you are experiencing a problem with posterizing or you did your editing on a monitor that is set too dark. Turn up the brightness and look just to the left of the face. The strong black area looks like it was made with a circle brush.</td>', 'Either you are experiencing a problem with posterizing or you did your editing on a monitor that is set too dark. Turn up the brightness and look just to the left of the face. The strong black area looks like it was made with a circle brush.', '2007-01-10 01:12:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3203376, 449466, 69776, '<td valign="top">too small, and hard to do well angle, almost straight up her nose, Good Luck 2</td>', 'too small, and hard to do well angle, almost straight up her nose, Good Luck 2', '2007-01-10 01:12:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(3203379, 447239, 47316, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous. Has a very simple and delacate feel. Oh ha! I just looked at the title after I wrote that. Fitting.<br/> <br/>Looks like something you would see in a lingerie store. I always try to leave a critique but it is hard because I really like this! So I''d say this might have done nicely with a bit of eye contact, even in just a shy way. Another thing is perhaps a more varied background, if it wasn''t for the arm being so close the edge I''d say possibly a very subtle vignette.</td>', 'Gorgeous. Has a very simple and delacate feel. Oh ha! I just looked at the title after I wrote that. Fitting. Looks like something you would see in a lingerie store. I always try to leave a critique but it is hard because I really like this! So I''d say this might have done nicely with a bit of eye contact, even in just a shy way. Another thing is perhaps a more varied background, if it wasn''t for the arm being so close the edge I''d say possibly a very subtle vignette.', '2007-01-10 01:13:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3203383, 449819, 19982, '<td valign="top">Should be "portrait of a pretty girl".  Very nicely done.  I like how the background surrounds and frames her with light.  It draws the eye right into the center of the image.  Love her expression and the lighting on her face.  Very nice b&amp;w treatment too.</td>', 'Should be "portrait of a pretty girl".  Very nicely done.  I like how the background surrounds and frames her with light.  It draws the eye right into the center of the image.  Love her expression and the lighting on her face.  Very nice b&w treatment too.', '2007-01-10 01:14:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3203385, 450627, 69776, '<td valign="top">The little girl is well lit but both parents are not, perhaps some dodge would have brought then out, Good Luck 4</td>', 'The little girl is well lit but both parents are not, perhaps some dodge would have brought then out, Good Luck 4', '2007-01-10 01:14:13.000000', NULL, 1),
