(3210493, 448537, 70187, '<td valign="top">I like the hair fading in the blackness behind. Very nice light falling on both eyes. I also like how the light brings out the texture in both hair and clothing. But somehow to me it looks like the focus was not on the most visible eye (on the right side of the photo) but on the mouth. vote=6</td>', 'I like the hair fading in the blackness behind. Very nice light falling on both eyes. I also like how the light brings out the texture in both hair and clothing. But somehow to me it looks like the focus was not on the most visible eye (on the right side of the photo) but on the mouth. vote=6', '2007-01-11 01:46:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210495, 448437, 16241, '<td valign="top">great!</td>', 'great!', '2007-01-11 01:49:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210496, 447611, 5347, '<td valign="top">deep</td>', 'deep', '2007-01-11 01:49:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210498, 449165, 71392, '<td valign="top">you can''t mask out of focus at the face with excessive softening and brightening. The focus went to the hair at the top.</td>', 'you can''t mask out of focus at the face with excessive softening and brightening. The focus went to the hair at the top.', '2007-01-11 01:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210499, 450784, 71392, '<td valign="top">really nice shot, too bad it got slightly cropped at the bottom.</td>', 'really nice shot, too bad it got slightly cropped at the bottom.', '2007-01-11 01:50:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210500, 448518, 70187, '<td valign="top">I like how this shot is different. Her make-up, hair-do, jewels and clothing all fit together nicely to create a special look, which is emphasized by her look. I like that you decided to take the photo from above.. a unique perspective which fit her. <br/> <br/>I don''t like how the second hand seems to drop in from the outside (right one on the photo). At first i didn''t have the idea it was one of hers really. I would have preferred it if it was connected to the body as the first one (left on the photo) is. vote=7</td>', 'I like how this shot is different. Her make-up, hair-do, jewels and clothing all fit together nicely to create a special look, which is emphasized by her look. I like that you decided to take the photo from above.. a unique perspective which fit her.  I don''t like how the second hand seems to drop in from the outside (right one on the photo). At first i didn''t have the idea it was one of hers really. I would have preferred it if it was connected to the body as the first one (left on the photo) is. vote=7', '2007-01-11 01:50:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210503, 449698, 66201, '<td valign="top">Just a preference on my part: the super close-up I find claustrophobic. It doesn''t tell anything about the person, you can''t read anything about the  moment, and the frame is filled with a lot of facial skin... I understand loads of people like this extreme close-up, but there it is. Nice lighting though.</td>', 'Just a preference on my part: the super close-up I find claustrophobic. It doesn''t tell anything about the person, you can''t read anything about the  moment, and the frame is filled with a lot of facial skin... I understand loads of people like this extreme close-up, but there it is. Nice lighting though.', '2007-01-11 01:52:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210504, 450225, 71392, '<td valign="top">too bright, which unfortunately also loses the cuteness of the dress.</td>', 'too bright, which unfortunately also loses the cuteness of the dress.', '2007-01-11 01:52:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210505, 447206, 71392, '<td valign="top">Not applicable to the contest theme.</td>', 'Not applicable to the contest theme.', '2007-01-11 01:53:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210507, 447294, 71392, '<td valign="top">More like "bright hair".</td>', 'More like "bright hair".', '2007-01-11 01:54:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210508, 450728, 66201, '<td valign="top">It''s hard to discern anything of the character of this subject: it''s so close up I cannot "read" anything from him. Half of his face is in complete darkness and the half that is lit, is so close up I can''t see hair, or if his chin goes straight down into his neck or not...he''s just half a frame of darkened skin at the moment. I understand that many like the extreme close up composition, so this is entirely subjective.</td>', 'It''s hard to discern anything of the character of this subject: it''s so close up I cannot "read" anything from him. Half of his face is in complete darkness and the half that is lit, is so close up I can''t see hair, or if his chin goes straight down into his neck or not...he''s just half a frame of darkened skin at the moment. I understand that many like the extreme close up composition, so this is entirely subjective.', '2007-01-11 01:55:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210509, 448593, 71392, '<td valign="top">A bit too static, maybe some (real) motion blur would have helped a lot. Otherwise, great black background, and great tone, balance and framing. 6</td>', 'A bit too static, maybe some (real) motion blur would have helped a lot. Otherwise, great black background, and great tone, balance and framing. 6', '2007-01-11 01:57:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210512, 450054, 71392, '<td valign="top">Slightly too bright PP, appealing smile and eyes. 6</td>', 'Slightly too bright PP, appealing smile and eyes. 6', '2007-01-11 01:59:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210513, 450642, 70187, '<td valign="top">Why did you put him to the right of the photo? He looks to the right, and instinctively i would say that the look needs more space on the right to give it more impact on us. Now you break the look in my opinion. <br/> <br/>I do like how the black hair goes into the background, connecting the two. At the same time the light gives us enough to feel the texture of the hair. The same goes for the clothing.. nice detail because of good use of light there.<br/> <br/>However i don''t like the light on his face, meaning it''s good on his face, but not eyes or vice versa. The white of the eyes looks darker than the skin, which doesn''t feel right. Maybe just a slight lightening of the white in the eyes? Also you have chosen for a very straight forward light, which in this case also means that his ear gets a lot of light. It''s a secondary attraction-point because the hair cuts it off of the face and thus you get two points of interest, damaging the impact of the face. If you had chosen to put your light slightly to the right of you, the ear would have been in the shadow and attract less attention.<br/> <br/>vote:5</td>', 'Why did you put him to the right of the photo? He looks to the right, and instinctively i would say that the look needs more space on the right to give it more impact on us. Now you break the look in my opinion.  I do like how the black hair goes into the background, connecting the two. At the same time the light gives us enough to feel the texture of the hair. The same goes for the clothing.. nice detail because of good use of light there. However i don''t like the light on his face, meaning it''s good on his face, but not eyes or vice versa. The white of the eyes looks darker than the skin, which doesn''t feel right. Maybe just a slight lightening of the white in the eyes? Also you have chosen for a very straight forward light, which in this case also means that his ear gets a lot of light. It''s a secondary attraction-point because the hair cuts it off of the face and thus you get two points of interest, damaging the impact of the face. If you had chosen to put your light slightly to the right of you, the ear would have been in the shadow and attract less attention. vote:5', '2007-01-11 01:59:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210514, 450862, 70187, '<td valign="top">People (including me) look to the brightest part of a photo.. it is natural. Here you see that that leads to the hand and not her face. I really do like your idea of letting the guitar leading you up to the face, but light should support this and not work against it in my opinion. vote=5</td>', 'People (including me) look to the brightest part of a photo.. it is natural. Here you see that that leads to the hand and not her face. I really do like your idea of letting the guitar leading you up to the face, but light should support this and not work against it in my opinion. vote=5', '2007-01-11 02:01:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3210519, 450754, 71392, '<td valign="top">hmm, where have I seen this face before...</td>', 'hmm, where have I seen this face before...', '2007-01-11 02:06:20.000000', NULL, 1),
