(3212594, 447567, 68947, '<td valign="top">Oh, have I seen that attitude! LOL  Parents KNOW that look.  My only constructive piece of advice on this would be that perhaps, the "highlights" are either too light or too dark and the "shadows" are a bit too dark.  But, I see your dilema where if you were to lighten the entire shot, you''d have the really highlighted area in the back of his hair and jawline, almost blanched.  Perhaps, a bit of "dodging" would have darkened that area and you could have lightened the brightness just a tad on the entire shot????</td>', 'Oh, have I seen that attitude! LOL  Parents KNOW that look.  My only constructive piece of advice on this would be that perhaps, the "highlights" are either too light or too dark and the "shadows" are a bit too dark.  But, I see your dilema where if you were to lighten the entire shot, you''d have the really highlighted area in the back of his hair and jawline, almost blanched.  Perhaps, a bit of "dodging" would have darkened that area and you could have lightened the brightness just a tad on the entire shot????', '2007-01-11 14:03:32.000000', NULL, 1),
