(3235082, 447350, 38127, '<td valign="top">K.. this picture appeals for so many reasons.. its dead sexy with those lips and slightly parted mouth.. her eyes are wicked.. the hair has a wild and free feel to it.. the tank and tattoo just speak volumes to the spirit of this woman.. this is one of my fav''s from the entire challenge. I might have lost the hand in the upper right.. but the tight crop is awesome here :)</td>', 'K.. this picture appeals for so many reasons.. its dead sexy with those lips and slightly parted mouth.. her eyes are wicked.. the hair has a wild and free feel to it.. the tank and tattoo just speak volumes to the spirit of this woman.. this is one of my fav''s from the entire challenge. I might have lost the hand in the upper right.. but the tight crop is awesome here :)', '2007-01-15 13:57:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3235083, 450818, 6388, '<td valign="top">Hellloooo, Denise :)<br/> <br/>a very nice moody portrait, Martin...rare to see D without a smile on her face.  For the purposes of DP (whose opinions are not always congruent with the rest of the world) I can offer a little insight: the slight overexposure on the left of the photo won''t go over all that well.  DP tends to favour perfect exposure, despite the fact that overexposure can often benefit an image.  The shadow cast  by her head adds a bit of an off-centred feel to the image; DP tends to favour more balanced images.  This isn''t to say that DP voters are always right (in fact, often they''re not), but since they are the masses we''re pandering to in these challenges it''s worth paying attention to.<br/> <br/>For my own personal opinion (DP aside), I like her off-centred, and i like that her face leads my eye to the centre of the photo.  The pose and expression are great, and there''s a real connection to the viewer.  As for the crop, I''d prefer it be either a bit tigher OR a bit looser - as it is, the top of the image acts as a bit of a ceiling and closes the image in a bit, making her head look a little elongated.  a tight crop that cuts off the top of her head or a looser one that adds some context might even out the perspective a little.<br/> <br/>Overall a solid photo and a good entry.  nice contrast and sharp focus on the right parts.  well done, M.<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'Hellloooo, Denise :) a very nice moody portrait, Martin...rare to see D without a smile on her face.  For the purposes of DP (whose opinions are not always congruent with the rest of the world) I can offer a little insight: the slight overexposure on the left of the photo won''t go over all that well.  DP tends to favour perfect exposure, despite the fact that overexposure can often benefit an image.  The shadow cast  by her head adds a bit of an off-centred feel to the image; DP tends to favour more balanced images.  This isn''t to say that DP voters are always right (in fact, often they''re not), but since they are the masses we''re pandering to in these challenges it''s worth paying attention to. For my own personal opinion (DP aside), I like her off-centred, and i like that her face leads my eye to the centre of the photo.  The pose and expression are great, and there''s a real connection to the viewer.  As for the crop, I''d prefer it be either a bit tigher OR a bit looser - as it is, the top of the image acts as a bit of a ceiling and closes the image in a bit, making her head look a little elongated.  a tight crop that cuts off the top of her head or a looser one that adds some context might even out the perspective a little. Overall a solid photo and a good entry.  nice contrast and sharp focus on the right parts.  well done, M. P', '2007-01-15 13:58:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(3235087, 447967, 59198, '<td valign="top">LMAO!!!! when I turned to this one I just had to laugh out loud...thank you<br/>I gave you an 8. A wonderful unigue portrait.</td>', 'LMAO!!!! when I turned to this one I just had to laugh out loud...thank youI gave you an 8. A wonderful unigue portrait.', '2007-01-15 13:59:11.000000', NULL, 1),
