(3251390, 448212, 69700, '<td valign="top">I like the intense look on the models face and especially in her eyes.  Good contrast.  I disagree with some of the others, I like the wind blown hair,</td>', 'I like the intense look on the models face and especially in her eyes.  Good contrast.  I disagree with some of the others, I like the wind blown hair,', '2007-01-18 12:15:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3251518, 448690, 57791, '<td valign="top">While I agree that the photo was a bit over blown I had alot of trouble getting the mothers foot to look good without really blowing the photo.<br/>So I was going for an angelic look. (The mothers foot was at least 10 shades darker then her kids)<br/> <br/>One unexpected benifit is that the photo actually looks much better like this when printed and thus the client loved it.<br/> <br/>Thank you for all the comments and yes it was my intention to try something a little different.<br/> <br/>The definition I used for this challenge is<br/><a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portrait" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Definition used</a> <br/> <br/>ps....who has perfectly smooth feet. I want to know what they use for lotion because I need some in a bad why..lol<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-18 13:05:16.</i></td>', 'While I agree that the photo was a bit over blown I had alot of trouble getting the mothers foot to look good without really blowing the photo.So I was going for an angelic look. (The mothers foot was at least 10 shades darker then her kids) One unexpected benifit is that the photo actually looks much better like this when printed and thus the client loved it. Thank you for all the comments and yes it was my intention to try something a little different. The definition I used for this challenge isDefinition used  ps....who has perfectly smooth feet. I want to know what they use for lotion because I need some in a bad why..lol', '2007-01-18 12:50:05.000000', '2007-01-18 13:05:16.000000', 0),
(3251781, 450156, 57060, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kelbelle:</b></div><hr/><i> yes, feeling of disconnect. Grammy looks like she''d rather be doing something else.  nice lighting though, and the baby looks very snuggly. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>In my mind this is what made the picture unique - the relationship between the GM and the child is not exactly heart warming, which sometimes happens, it''s a very real and unique perspective which I believe took courage to show. I really liked this the first time, but didn''t think it would do too well due the perspective most people bring to these kind of shots - again well done.<br/> <br/>Jack</td>', 'Originally posted by kelbelle: yes, feeling of disconnect. Grammy looks like she''d rather be doing something else.  nice lighting though, and the baby looks very snuggly.   In my mind this is what made the picture unique - the relationship between the GM and the child is not exactly heart warming, which sometimes happens, it''s a very real and unique perspective which I believe took courage to show. I really liked this the first time, but didn''t think it would do too well due the perspective most people bring to these kind of shots - again well done. Jack', '2007-01-18 14:16:40.000000', NULL, 0),
