(3269686, 450389, 70828, '<td valign="top">Did I ever mention that I thought that this was a drop dead gorgeous image?<br/> <br/>IMO that is SO close to a blue ribbon winner that it makes my skin itch!<br/> <br/>Bring on the flutes and clarinets ... It will work SO well with that treatment. Saxophones ... even better.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-23 04:23:15.</i></td>', 'Did I ever mention that I thought that this was a drop dead gorgeous image? IMO that is SO close to a blue ribbon winner that it makes my skin itch! Bring on the flutes and clarinets ... It will work SO well with that treatment. Saxophones ... even better.', '2007-01-23 04:14:01.000000', '2007-01-23 04:23:15.000000', 0),
(3269839, 450245, 55838, '<td valign="top">Great shot Hanae.  Cool subject and nice framing.  Good score.  My eyes would love to see a stronger gradient in the background (light around his face just the way you have it, then gradually much darker as the eye moves away from the man toward the edges of the photo). Excellent model and a very nice job!</td>', 'Great shot Hanae.  Cool subject and nice framing.  Good score.  My eyes would love to see a stronger gradient in the background (light around his face just the way you have it, then gradually much darker as the eye moves away from the man toward the edges of the photo). Excellent model and a very nice job!', '2007-01-23 05:38:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3270406, 450770, 53018, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your yellow!</td>', 'Congratulations on your yellow!', '2007-01-23 09:54:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3270733, 449348, 58728, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely portrait.  The composition is very nice.  The reason I think it may have not scored better would be the lighting on her face. Her face looks a bit dark, but the background looks a bit too light.  It''s a bit too contrasty. It''s a lovely shot, but maybe could use just a bit more light on her face.  :)</td>', 'This is a lovely portrait.  The composition is very nice.  The reason I think it may have not scored better would be the lighting on her face. Her face looks a bit dark, but the background looks a bit too light.  It''s a bit too contrasty. It''s a lovely shot, but maybe could use just a bit more light on her face.  :)', '2007-01-23 12:21:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3270756, 449348, 13207, '<td valign="top">It''s definitely not a bad shot by any means.  I too think the contrast is a little too high, especially evident on her shoulder on the left side.  I think also that this shot may have scored better with a closer crop, less background and less along the bottom.  Finally, there also seems to be some markings in the top right corner - not sure if it''s from post-processing or actual shadows on your background.</td>', 'It''s definitely not a bad shot by any means.  I too think the contrast is a little too high, especially evident on her shoulder on the left side.  I think also that this shot may have scored better with a closer crop, less background and less along the bottom.  Finally, there also seems to be some markings in the top right corner - not sure if it''s from post-processing or actual shadows on your background.', '2007-01-23 12:30:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3270793, 449348, 70828, '<td valign="top">I too find the contrast too jarring. I also find (I hope not to insult) that your model has too much eye makeup on. I do not think it suits her already elegant and pretty face.</td>', 'I too find the contrast too jarring. I also find (I hope not to insult) that your model has too much eye makeup on. I do not think it suits her already elegant and pretty face.', '2007-01-23 12:42:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3270800, 448178, 68388, '<td valign="top">I gave this one an 8 , it''s a great photo.  Did you use multiple flashes / light sources ?</td>', 'I gave this one an 8 , it''s a great photo.  Did you use multiple flashes / light sources ?', '2007-01-23 12:46:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3270803, 449766, 68388, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  Beautiful photo and model.  However, I am not 100% sure you''re trying to create a soft image or if the photo is out of focus.  Maybe it''s my monitor.  Nice work !</td>', 'I gave this an 8.  Beautiful photo and model.  However, I am not 100% sure you''re trying to create a soft image or if the photo is out of focus.  Maybe it''s my monitor.  Nice work !', '2007-01-23 12:48:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3270820, 450851, 72433, '<td valign="top">i really like this one!!!</td>', 'i really like this one!!!', '2007-01-23 12:53:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3270855, 449348, 28261, '<td valign="top">Interestingly, I find the contrast to be too high. (yup)  The boa shadows are too dark, or way too white - loss of major detail here.<br/> <br/>The problem appears to be the placement and intensity of the rear light, causing blowouts on the left and not enough dynamic range in the front.<br/> <br/>Yes, your wife''s eye liner is way too thick in this, giving her hollow eyes (post processing?)  <br/> <br/>Most if not all of the image could have benefited from a single additional over the head ( toward front ) light that allowed you to properly expose the face while not having to blow out that left side area.<br/> <br/>Overall, tho, lighting aside - very nice image, composure, model and pose.</td>', 'Interestingly, I find the contrast to be too high. (yup)  The boa shadows are too dark, or way too white - loss of major detail here. The problem appears to be the placement and intensity of the rear light, causing blowouts on the left and not enough dynamic range in the front. Yes, your wife''s eye liner is way too thick in this, giving her hollow eyes (post processing?)   Most if not all of the image could have benefited from a single additional over the head ( toward front ) light that allowed you to properly expose the face while not having to blow out that left side area. Overall, tho, lighting aside - very nice image, composure, model and pose.', '2007-01-23 13:04:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3271325, 450770, 72515, '<td valign="top">congradulations! I love this one. good job getting her eyes!</td>', 'congradulations! I love this one. good job getting her eyes!', '2007-01-23 15:33:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3271515, 450245, 45475, '<td valign="top">Way to go with your score Hanae! Great b&amp;w portrait. You just keep getting better and better!</td>', 'Way to go with your score Hanae! Great b&w portrait. You just keep getting better and better!', '2007-01-23 16:26:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3272216, 450737, 42013, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>First... This photo definitely caught my eye when browsing the entries. It''s certainly a fun, relaxed, ''impromptu'' portrait. And it is BW! ;)<br/> <br/>From a technical standpoint it could use a slight bump in contrast. Focus seems a little soft as well. The lighting is nice, leaving some shadow areas on the left side of the frame for depth. Good catchlights in the eyes.<br/> <br/>I like the 100% black BG and it''s possible that a radically off centered crop would have been good. Either leave Steveie in the center and go with a square crop like one of the commentators suggested or crop most of the black space from the left which would leave stevie looking pretty off-balance!<br/> <br/>As it relates to the challenge... Pretty hard not to meet the requirements of the challenge, so the technicals became that much more important. <br/> <br/>It''s wierd in a good way. Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>Mark</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club. First... This photo definitely caught my eye when browsing the entries. It''s certainly a fun, relaxed, ''impromptu'' portrait. And it is BW! ;) From a technical standpoint it could use a slight bump in contrast. Focus seems a little soft as well. The lighting is nice, leaving some shadow areas on the left side of the frame for depth. Good catchlights in the eyes. I like the 100% black BG and it''s possible that a radically off centered crop would have been good. Either leave Steveie in the center and go with a square crop like one of the commentators suggested or crop most of the black space from the left which would leave stevie looking pretty off-balance! As it relates to the challenge... Pretty hard not to meet the requirements of the challenge, so the technicals became that much more important.  It''s wierd in a good way. Keep up the good work. Mark', '2007-01-23 19:30:28.000000', NULL, 0),
